  "notes": "Godan verb derived from {遠|とお}い (distant). Conjugates as {遠|とお}のく・{遠|とお}のいて・{遠|とお}のいた.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {足|あし}が{遠|とお}のく (visits become less frequent)\n- {音|おと}が{遠|とお}のく (a sound fades away)\n- {意識|いしき}が{遠|とお}のく (consciousness fades — feeling faint)\n- {客|きゃく}が{遠|とお}のく (customers stop coming)\n\nThe idiom {足|あし}が{遠|とお}のく is particularly common, meaning someone visits or goes to a place less and less often. {意識|いしき}が{遠|とお}のく describes the sensation of losing consciousness.",
